  <prompt>Owner UAT round 6 (2026-10-06), item 4, plus the label observation in note §3. Record: `notes/042-uat-round6-2026-10-06.md`.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer on the Office add-in (React 19, Fluent UI v9).</role>

  <goal>Find shows two independent lists — Similar Documents and Matching records — that each scroll on their own and share the pane through a divider the user can drag, so neither list pushes the other out of view.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      - **Owner (round 6, item 4)**: separate sections for "Most similar documents" (rename **"Similar Documents"**)
        and "Matching records", each its own scrollable list; "each section dragable to …" (cut off). Main-session
        reading, stated to the owner: a **draggable divider** between the two sections that resizes their heights.
      - **Today** (tasks 092/077/034): one scroll for both lists; documents render progressively as the user scrolls
        (ADR-051 exception, spec row) and records page on "non-empty ⇒ more" (spec ADR-051 records row). Both
        progressive-scroll mechanisms must keep working inside their own scroll container.
      - **Item 5 (task 103)** hides the pane's main scroll bar, so each Find list's own scroll is what the user uses.
      - **Label observation (note §3)**: the pinned row reads "Matter: **Matter**" (record name shown as the type) and
        every similar document shows "**Unknown** · …" for its type. Find where each label comes from (client mapping
        vs. BFF response) and fix it if it is client-side; if the BFF sends no type/name, REPORT it.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner item 4">Two sections with headers "Similar Documents" and "Matching records"; each list scrolls independently; the pinned "this document's record" row stays with Similar Documents.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner item 4 (as interpreted)">A divider between the sections can be dragged (pointer) and moved with the keyboard (arrow keys; `role="separator"`, `aria-orientation="horizontal"`, `aria-valuenow`); each section keeps a minimum height so neither disappears; the split starts at an even share of the available height. The chosen split may be remembered per viewer (localStorage, wrapped in try/catch).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-051 exceptions">Progressive reveal (documents) and page-on-non-empty (records) keep working, each triggered by its own list's scroll; their existing tests stay green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-10 / ADR-021">Same in both hosts; Fluent v9 tokens; dark mode; works at 320 px and when the pane is wide (task 103).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Update the Find tests; add tests for the split and the divider; report new suites to the main session for `ci-gated-suites.txt`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Find shows "Similar Documents" and "Matching records" as two sections, each with its own scroll container.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dragging the divider (pointer) and pressing Up/Down on it (keyboard) changes the two heights; neither goes below its minimum.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Scrolling the documents list reveals more documents; scrolling the records list loads the next page — independently.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The label observation is resolved: the pinned row shows the record's name and type correctly, and documents show a real type where one exists; or the note records why not (server data) with evidence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: jest (all suites) green; lint 0; typecheck 0 production.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Live (after deploy): as above. If unavailable, leave open.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read the round-6 note, the 092/077 notes, `FindView.tsx`, `FindResultsList.tsx`, the Find hooks.</step>
    <step>Two sections + independent scroll; tests.</step>
    <step>Divider (pointer + keyboard); tests.</step>
    <step>Label check; gates; `notes/102-find-split-sections.md`; POML status.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>The Find view, both lists and their progressive loading exist (tasks 034/077/092).</existing>
    <extension>Yes — re-arranges the existing lists into two scroll regions with a divider. Check `@spaarke/ui-components` for an existing splitter/resizable-panel component first (ADR-012 amended: reuse by default) and use it by exact-path alias if one fits.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Owner UAT round 6 item 4: one long scroll hides Matching records below every similar document.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Find split">
      <steps>
        <step>Find: two sections; scroll each independently; drag the divider; Tab to it and use the arrow keys.</step>
      </steps>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

